      grammarExamples: <String>["If homes spread farther apart, journeys would become longer.", "A compact layout could help if services were adequate.", "If the projection changed, planners would revise the phases."],
      listening: "The proposed housing expansion will be assessed against several population scenarios, not only the highest growth estimate. Planners must consider when schools, transport, and water services can support additional residents. A site with cheaper land may still impose higher long-term costs if it requires extensive new infrastructure or longer journeys. Public comments should identify local access needs and the effects on existing communities. The final plan will link later phases to infrastructure milestones and will be reviewed if underlying assumptions change. Approval of the overall idea does not mean every phase should proceed regardless of service capacity.",
      listeningQuestion: "What will control later development phases?",
      listeningOptions: <String>["Infrastructure milestones and reviewed assumptions", "The highest population estimate alone", "The lowest land price regardless of services"],
      listeningAnswer: 0,
      readingQuestion: "Why was the cheaper land option not automatically preferable?",
      readingOptions: <String>["All public services were already unlimited", "It could create higher infrastructure and travel costs", "It had no space for housing"],
      readingAnswer: 1,
      writingCue: "A rapidly growing town approved a ____ beyond its existing center.",
      writingAnswer: "housing expansion",
    ),
    EnglishAdvancedLesson(
      level: "B2",
      unitNumber: 3,
      number: 7,
      title: "Rethinking the Exam System",
      titleArabic: "إعادة التفكير في الامتحانات",
      storyTitle: "Rethinking the Exam System",
      storyTitleArabic: "إعادة التفكير في الامتحانات",
      paragraphs: <String>["A college reviewed an exam system dominated by one final test. Teachers questioned whether a single timed performance captured the range of understanding developed throughout the course.", "An assessment working group compared continuous assessment with a final examination. A marking rubric could improve consistency, but repeated projects might increase workload and create more opportunities for outside assistance.", "The college piloted a balanced assessment using an oral explanation, a supervised task, and a written project. A moderation process compared marking decisions, while an appeals procedure allowed students to question possible errors.", "The review distinguished assessment reliability from the validity of what was measured. A consistent score was useful, but it did not guarantee that the assessment represented the skills the course claimed to develop."],
      storyWords: <EnglishAdvancedWord>[EnglishAdvancedWord("exam system", "نظام امتحانات"), EnglishAdvancedWord("final test", "اختبار نهائي"), EnglishAdvancedWord("timed performance", "أداء محدد الزمن"), EnglishAdvancedWord("assessment working group", "فريق عمل التقييم"), EnglishAdvancedWord("continuous assessment", "تقييم مستمر"), EnglishAdvancedWord("final examination", "امتحان ختامي"), EnglishAdvancedWord("marking rubric", "سلم تقدير"), EnglishAdvancedWord("outside assistance", "مساعدة خارجية"), EnglishAdvancedWord("balanced assessment", "تقييم متوازن"), EnglishAdvancedWord("oral explanation", "شرح شفهي"), EnglishAdvancedWord("supervised task", "مهمة مراقبة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("moderation process", "عملية معايرة التصحيح"), EnglishAdvancedWord("appeals procedure", "إجراء التظلمات"), EnglishAdvancedWord("assessment reliability", "ثبات التقييم")],
      extraWords: <EnglishAdvancedWord>[EnglishAdvancedWord("assessment validity", "صدق التقييم"), EnglishAdvancedWord("marking consistency", "اتساق التصحيح"), EnglishAdvancedWord("examination pressure", "ضغط الامتحان"), EnglishAdvancedWord("learning outcomes", "نواتج التعلم"), EnglishAdvancedWord("coursework assessment", "تقييم أعمال المقرر"), EnglishAdvancedWord("grading criterion", "معيار التقدير"), EnglishAdvancedWord("oral defense", "مناقشة شفوية"), EnglishAdvancedWord("assessment workload", "عبء التقييم"), EnglishAdvancedWord("student appeal", "تظلم طالب"), EnglishAdvancedWord("scoring guide", "دليل الدرجات"), EnglishAdvancedWord("exam preparation", "استعداد الامتحان"), EnglishAdvancedWord("independent performance", "أداء مستقل"), EnglishAdvancedWord("assessment balance", "توازن التقييم"), EnglishAdvancedWord("test anxiety", "قلق الاختبار"), EnglishAdvancedWord("marking review", "مراجعة التصحيح"), EnglishAdvancedWord("skills coverage", "تغطية المهارات"), EnglishAdvancedWord("evaluation method", "طريقة التقييم"), EnglishAdvancedWord("assessment evidence", "أدلة التقييم"), EnglishAdvancedWord("grading fairness", "عدالة الدرجات"), EnglishAdvancedWord("exam format", "شكل الامتحان"), EnglishAdvancedWord("performance criterion", "معيار الأداء"), EnglishAdvancedWord("assessment purpose", "غرض التقييم")],
      grammarTitle: "Although, despite and however",
      grammarArabic: "تأتي although قبل جملة كاملة، بينما تأتي despite قبل اسم أو ing. تستخدم however للربط بين جملتين متعارضتين مع ترقيم مناسب.",
      grammarExamples: <String>["Although scores were consistent, some skills were not measured.", "Despite its benefits, coursework increased workload.", "The exam was reliable; however, its coverage was narrow."],
      listening: "The assessment pilot will combine a supervised task, a written project, and a short oral explanation. Each component is intended to reveal a different aspect of learning. Students will receive the marking criteria in advance, and a moderation group will compare examples to improve consistency. The review will consider workload and access to outside help as well as the final scores. Please remember that a reliable assessment produces reasonably consistent judgments, while a valid assessment measures the intended skills. Neither quality should be assumed merely because a method is traditional, familiar, or easy to score.",
      listeningQuestion: "What is the distinction explained by the speaker?",
      listeningOptions: <String>["Traditional tests automatically possess both", "Reliability concerns consistency; validity concerns intended skills", "Reliability and validity mean easy scoring"],
      listeningAnswer: 1,
      readingQuestion: "Why did the pilot use several components?",
      readingOptions: <String>["To eliminate all marking criteria", "To guarantee that no student would appeal", "To assess different aspects of learning"],
      readingAnswer: 2,
      writingCue: "A college reviewed an ____ dominated by one final test.",
      writingAnswer: "exam system",
    ),
    EnglishAdvancedLesson(
      level: "B2",
      unitNumber: 3,
      number: 8,
      title: "Citizens and Open Data",
      titleArabic: "المواطنون والبيانات المفتوحة",
      storyTitle: "Citizens and Open Data",
      storyTitleArabic: "المواطنون والبيانات المفتوحة",
      paragraphs: <String>["A city published an open dataset showing repair requests by neighborhood. A civic analyst created a public dashboard, but its neighborhood comparison appeared to rank some areas as unusually neglected.", "The analyst discovered that reporting rates differed because residents used different channels. A raw request count could reflect active reporting rather than the actual number of faults, especially where telephone complaints were missing.", "A data-quality note explained the missing fields and inconsistent categories. The city added a machine-readable file and a revision log, while removing personal details that were not needed for public analysis.", "The updated dashboard showed a cautious comparison and invited correction requests. Its creators argued that open access was valuable only when users could understand the data's origin, limits, and appropriate uses."],
      storyWords: <EnglishAdvancedWord>[EnglishAdvancedWord("open dataset", "مجموعة بيانات مفتوحة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("repair requests", "طلبات إصلاح"), EnglishAdvancedWord("civic analyst", "محلل مدني"), EnglishAdvancedWord("public dashboard", "لوحة عامة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("neighborhood comparison", "مقارنة الأحياء"), EnglishAdvancedWord("reporting rates", "معدلات الإبلاغ"), EnglishAdvancedWord("raw request count", "عدد الطلبات الخام"), EnglishAdvancedWord("telephone complaints", "شكاوى هاتفية"), EnglishAdvancedWord("data-quality note", "ملاحظة جودة البيانات"), EnglishAdvancedWord("missing fields", "حقول مفقودة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("inconsistent categories", "فئات غير متسقة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("machine-readable file", "ملف قابل للقراءة الآلية"), EnglishAdvancedWord("revision log", "سجل التعديلات"), EnglishAdvancedWord("correction requests", "طلبات تصحيح")],
      extraWords: <EnglishAdvancedWord>[EnglishAdvancedWord("open data", "بيانات مفتوحة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("data provenance", "منشأ البيانات"), EnglishAdvancedWord("reporting channel", "قناة الإبلاغ"), EnglishAdvancedWord("data documentation", "توثيق البيانات"), EnglishAdvancedWord("category definition", "تعريف الفئة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("missing data", "بيانات مفقودة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("data completeness", "اكتمال البيانات"), EnglishAdvancedWord("public analysis", "تحليل عام"), EnglishAdvancedWord("reusable format", "صيغة قابلة لإعادة الاستخدام"), EnglishAdvancedWord("data release", "نشر البيانات"), EnglishAdvancedWord("privacy protection", "حماية الخصوصية"), EnglishAdvancedWord("data revision", "تعديل البيانات"), EnglishAdvancedWord("reporting difference", "اختلاف الإبلاغ"), EnglishAdvancedWord("comparison limit", "حد المقارنة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("measurement coverage", "تغطية القياس"), EnglishAdvancedWord("civic technology", "تقنية مدنية"), EnglishAdvancedWord("dataset update", "تحديث البيانات"), EnglishAdvancedWord("raw count", "عدد خام"), EnglishAdvancedWord("data explanation", "شرح البيانات"), EnglishAdvancedWord("public feedback", "ملاحظات عامة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("data quality", "جودة البيانات"), EnglishAdvancedWord("responsible reuse", "إعادة استخدام مسؤولة")],
      grammarTitle: "Passive voice",
      grammarArabic: "نستخدم be مع التصريف الثالث لإبراز الفعل أو المتأثر به. يتغير be حسب الزمن. نذكر الفاعل بعد by فقط عندما تكون معرفته مهمة.",
      grammarExamples: <String>["Telephone complaints were omitted from the first dataset.", "Categories have been clarified in the notes.", "Personal details must be removed before release."],
      listening: "The repair-request dataset is now available in a reusable format with documentation and a revision log. Users should not interpret the number of requests as a direct measure of all maintenance problems. Reporting channels differ, and some categories are incomplete in the earliest months. The dashboard therefore labels comparisons that may be misleading and links to the relevant notes. If you identify an error, submit a correction request with the record reference and your reason. Personal information has been removed because public scrutiny of service patterns does not require identifying the residents who made individual complaints.",
      listeningQuestion: "Why is request count not a direct measure of all faults?",
      listeningOptions: <String>["Every complaint is invented", "The data contains only photographs", "Reporting channels and completeness differ"],
      listeningAnswer: 2,
      readingQuestion: "What made the updated dashboard more responsible?",
      readingOptions: <String>["It explained limits and accepted correction requests", "It hid missing fields", "It published residents' private details"],
      readingAnswer: 0,
      writingCue: "A city published an ____ showing repair requests by neighborhood.",
      writingAnswer: "open dataset",
    ),
    EnglishAdvancedLesson(
      level: "B2",
      unitNumber: 3,
      number: 9,
      title: "Economic Opportunity and Risk",
      titleArabic: "الفرص الاقتصادية والمخاطر",
      storyTitle: "Economic Opportunity and Risk",
      storyTitleArabic: "الفرص الاقتصادية والمخاطر",
      paragraphs: <String>["A regional workshop examined a fictional proposal for a new logistics hub. Supporters emphasized job creation and supplier demand, while the feasibility report acknowledged uncertain transport costs and customer commitments.", "An economist presented a best-case scenario alongside a downside scenario. The employment estimate depended on several assumptions, including how much work would be automated and whether firms would hire locally.", "Participants reviewed a sensitivity analysis showing which assumptions most affected the outcome. A phased investment could limit exposure, but it would also delay some benefits and could not remove every commercial risk.", "The group recommended a conditional decision with a review trigger before the next phase. Their conclusion distinguished a promising opportunity from a guaranteed return and asked who would bear the costs if the forecast proved too optimistic."],
      storyWords: <EnglishAdvancedWord>[EnglishAdvancedWord("logistics hub", "مركز لوجستي"), EnglishAdvancedWord("job creation", "خلق الوظائف"), EnglishAdvancedWord("supplier demand", "طلب الموردين"), EnglishAdvancedWord("feasibility report", "تقرير الجدوى"), EnglishAdvancedWord("customer commitments", "التزامات العملاء"), EnglishAdvancedWord("best-case scenario", "أفضل سيناريو"), EnglishAdvancedWord("downside scenario", "سيناريو سلبي"), EnglishAdvancedWord("employment estimate", "تقدير التوظيف"), EnglishAdvancedWord("sensitivity analysis", "تحليل الحساسية"), EnglishAdvancedWord("phased investment", "استثمار مرحلي"), EnglishAdvancedWord("commercial risk", "مخاطر تجارية"), EnglishAdvancedWord("review trigger", "شرط بدء المراجعة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("guaranteed return", "عائد مضمون"), EnglishAdvancedWord("conditional decision", "قرار مشروط")],
      extraWords: <EnglishAdvancedWord>[EnglishAdvancedWord("economic opportunity", "فرصة اقتصادية"), EnglishAdvancedWord("forecast assumption", "افتراض التوقع"), EnglishAdvancedWord("investment phase", "مرحلة استثمار"), EnglishAdvancedWord("risk exposure", "انكشاف للمخاطر"), EnglishAdvancedWord("local employment", "توظيف محلي"), EnglishAdvancedWord("demand estimate", "تقدير الطلب"), EnglishAdvancedWord("economic scenario", "سيناريو اقتصادي"), EnglishAdvancedWord("cost uncertainty", "عدم يقين التكلفة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("public investment", "استثمار عام"), EnglishAdvancedWord("commercial viability", "جدوى تجارية"), EnglishAdvancedWord("benefit estimate", "تقدير المنفعة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("scenario comparison", "مقارنة السيناريوهات"), EnglishAdvancedWord("risk allocation", "توزيع المخاطر"), EnglishAdvancedWord("optimistic forecast", "توقع متفائل"), EnglishAdvancedWord("investment condition", "شرط الاستثمار"), EnglishAdvancedWord("employment impact", "أثر التوظيف"), EnglishAdvancedWord("business demand", "طلب الأعمال"), EnglishAdvancedWord("cost overrun", "تجاوز التكلفة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("contingency reserve", "احتياطي طوارئ"), EnglishAdvancedWord("economic assessment", "تقييم اقتصادي"), EnglishAdvancedWord("forecast sensitivity", "حساسية التوقع"), EnglishAdvancedWord("decision checkpoint", "نقطة مراجعة القرار")],
      grammarTitle: "Second conditional",
      grammarArabic: "نستخدم if مع الماضي البسيط وwould مع الفعل الأساسي لافتراض غير واقعي أو غير محتمل في الحاضر أو المستقبل. يمكن استخدام were مع جميع الضمائر في الافتراض.",
      grammarExamples: <String>["If demand fell, the hub would create fewer jobs.", "A phased approach would limit exposure if costs rose.", "If automation increased, staffing needs could change."],
      listening: "This fictional economic assessment compares several possible outcomes for a logistics project. The central forecast assumes a particular level of customer demand and local recruitment, but those assumptions are not commitments. Participants should examine how changes in costs, automation, or demand affect the estimated benefits. A phased approach may reduce exposure, although it can also postpone gains. The task is to explain the conditions under which the proposal appears reasonable and identify who carries the downside risk. Do not describe the central forecast as a guaranteed result simply because it is presented in a detailed spreadsheet.",
      listeningQuestion: "What should participants avoid?",
      listeningOptions: <String>["Treating a central forecast as guaranteed", "Comparing different assumptions", "Identifying who bears downside risk"],
      listeningAnswer: 0,
      readingQuestion: "Why did the group recommend a review trigger?",
      readingOptions: <String>["To guarantee the best-case outcome", "To reassess conditions before the next phase", "To eliminate every commercial risk"],
      readingAnswer: 1,
      writingCue: "A regional workshop examined a fictional proposal for a new ____.",
      writingAnswer: "logistics hub",
    ),
    EnglishAdvancedLesson(
      level: "B2",
      unitNumber: 3,
      number: 10,
      title: "A Balanced Policy Review",
      titleArabic: "مراجعة متوازنة لسياسة عامة",
      storyTitle: "A Balanced Policy Review",
      storyTitleArabic: "مراجعة متوازنة لسياسة عامة",
      paragraphs: <String>["A town evaluated a year-long library access policy intended to extend evening use. The evaluation brief asked whether additional opening hours had reached people previously unable to attend, not simply increased total visits.", "An evaluator compared an attendance baseline with the trial figures and interviewed non-users. A positive average concealed uneven uptake across neighborhoods, while the staffing record showed unplanned overtime during the busiest months.", "The policy review separated implementation problems from weaknesses in the original objective. A counterfactual question asked what might have happened without the change, though the evidence could not establish that alternative with certainty.", "The final recommendation supported a revised continuation with targeted outreach and a staffing adjustment. It included a limitation statement and a future review point, showing how a balanced judgment could recommend action while remaining honest about unresolved evidence."],
      storyWords: <EnglishAdvancedWord>[EnglishAdvancedWord("library access policy", "سياسة الوصول للمكتبة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("evaluation brief", "موجز التقييم"), EnglishAdvancedWord("additional opening hours", "ساعات فتح إضافية"), EnglishAdvancedWord("attendance baseline", "خط أساس الحضور"), EnglishAdvancedWord("trial figures", "أرقام التجربة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("non-users", "غير المستخدمين"), EnglishAdvancedWord("positive average", "متوسط إيجابي"), EnglishAdvancedWord("uneven uptake", "إقبال غير متساوٍ"), EnglishAdvancedWord("staffing record", "سجل الموظفين"), EnglishAdvancedWord("unplanned overtime", "عمل إضافي غير مخطط"), EnglishAdvancedWord("counterfactual question", "سؤال عن بديل لم يقع"), EnglishAdvancedWord("targeted outreach", "تواصل موجه"), EnglishAdvancedWord("staffing adjustment", "تعديل الموظفين"), EnglishAdvancedWord("limitation statement", "بيان القيود")],
      extraWords: <EnglishAdvancedWord>[EnglishAdvancedWord("policy evaluation", "تقييم السياسة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("evaluation objective", "هدف التقييم"), EnglishAdvancedWord("outcome indicator", "مؤشر النتيجة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("implementation problem", "مشكلة التنفيذ"), EnglishAdvancedWord("comparison period", "فترة المقارنة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("unintended consequence", "نتيجة غير مقصودة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("distributional effect", "أثر توزيعي"), EnglishAdvancedWord("evidence gap", "فجوة أدلة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("balanced recommendation", "توصية متوازنة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("policy continuation", "استمرار السياسة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("review framework", "إطار المراجعة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("counterfactual comparison", "مقارنة ببديل افتراضي"), EnglishAdvancedWord("policy effectiveness", "فعالية السياسة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("evaluation criteria", "معايير التقييم"), EnglishAdvancedWord("outreach strategy", "استراتيجية التواصل"), EnglishAdvancedWord("staffing adjustment plan", "خطة تعديل الموظفين"), EnglishAdvancedWord("qualified conclusion", "خلاصة مقيدة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("outcome uncertainty", "عدم يقين النتيجة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("evaluation transparency", "شفافية التقييم"), EnglishAdvancedWord("policy learning", "تعلم من السياسات"), EnglishAdvancedWord("review cycle", "دورة المراجعة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("implementation evidence", "أدلة التنفيذ")],
      grammarTitle: "Third conditional",
      grammarArabic: "نستخدم if + had + التصريف الثالث، ثم would have + التصريف الثالث لتخيل نتيجة بديلة لحدث ماضٍ لم يقع كما نتخيله.",
      grammarExamples: <String>["If the team had counted only visits, it would have missed uneven access.", "The policy might have reached more residents if outreach had started earlier.", "If staffing had been planned differently, overtime might have been lower."],
      listening: "The final review should assess the library policy against its stated objective of widening access. Higher total attendance is relevant, but it does not establish that previously excluded residents have benefited. Compare the trial with the baseline, consider who still does not attend, and examine staffing costs alongside visitor feedback. Your recommendation may support continuation, revision, or withdrawal, provided it follows from the evidence. Include a limitation statement explaining what the evaluation cannot determine. A balanced conclusion is not a refusal to decide; it is a decision whose reasons, conditions, and remaining uncertainties are visible to the reader.",
      listeningQuestion: "What makes a conclusion balanced in this review?",
      listeningOptions: <String>["Using only the total attendance figure", "Visible reasons, conditions, and uncertainties", "Refusing to recommend any action"],
      listeningAnswer: 1,
      readingQuestion: "What did the review recommend?",
      readingOptions: <String>["Immediate expansion without conditions", "Ignoring uneven neighborhood uptake", "Revised continuation with outreach and staffing changes"],
      readingAnswer: 2,
      writingCue: "A town evaluated a year-long ____ intended to extend evening use.",
      writingAnswer: "library access policy",
    ),
  ];
}
